  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">HD Flexibelt medlingsinitiativ 2019-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HD Flexible Mediation Initiative 2019-2022 - CHD mediation initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Centre for Humanitarian Dialogue (HD) har till Sida inkommit med en ans&#xf6;kan f&#xf6;r att erh&#xe5;lla 40 MSEK f&#xf6;r att finansiera Flexible Mediation Initiative (Sv: Flexibelt medlingsinitiativ), under 2019 - 2021. Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let med insatsen &#xe4;r att bidra till f&#xf6;rsoning mellan parterna i v&#xe4;pnande konflikter eller n&#xe4;r det finns ett betydande hot om v&#xe5;ld i en politisk eller humanit&#xe4;r kris. De olika projekten som utg&#xf6;r programmet Flexible Mediation Initiative har sina egna kontext specifika m&#xe5;l. De l&#xe4;nder eller kontexter som kommer f&#xe5; st&#xf6;d under det f&#xf6;reslagna programmet kan komma att &#xe4;ndras under de tre &#xe5;r som programmet kommer att implementeras.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Center for Humanitarian Dialogue (HD) has submitted an application to Sida for SEK 40 million to finance the Flexible Mediation Initiative, 2019 - 2021. The overall goal of the programme is to contribute to reconciliation between the parties in ongoing violent crises or when there is a significant threat of violence in a political or humanitarian crisis. The various projects that make up the Flexible Mediation Initiative program have their own specific objectives. The countries or contexts that will receive support under the proposed programme may change during the three years that the program will be implemented.</narrative>
  </description>
